-- check/good: an inferred type 300 constructors deep — comfortably under
-- `Schemes.Writer.max_depth` (512), so the whole scheme reaches the
-- interface and `check` exits 0 with nothing to say.
--
-- The `.iface` golden is the assertion, and what it pins is the scan that
-- decides whether a solved type is poisoned (§7). That scan used to carry a
-- FIXED 256-entry worklist and answer "too wide to tell" past it, and the
-- caller published `<error>` for this declaration without a word. An
-- interface entry that says `<error>` for a program the checker just
-- accepted is the exit-0 wrongness of §5: every importer then checks
-- against a hole.
--
-- The nesting leans RIGHT on purpose. The scan is depth-first over a stack,
-- so a left-nested `( ( 1, 2 ), 2 )` pops its leaf before it descends and
-- the stack never grows; a right-nested one leaves a leaf behind at every
-- level, which is the shape that reached the bound — as does an ordinary
-- record extension chain, one frame per link.
--
-- `Render` still truncates the PRINTED form at `Render.max_depth`, which is
-- the `…` in the golden and is only about how much of one type is shown.
